-- ▶ Application harness + classical cross-check: crates/apps/circulant/src/lib.rs
--   run: cargo run -p aria-app-circulant   (or: cargo run -p aria-verify -- circulant)
-- VERIFIED: per-basis-state output map of Q vs the exact cyclic permutation σ(x)=(x+1) mod 8; 0 mismatches and min purity ≥ 0.99, |Δ| = 0.
--
-- Cyclic-shift generator Q of a circulant matrix: |x⟩ → |x+1 mod 8⟩.
--
-- A banded circulant C = Σⱼ cⱼ·Q^{powⱼ} (e.g. the 1-D heat-transfer operator
-- (−2−ξ)I + Q + Q⁻¹) is a linear combination of powers of this single
-- generator, which the QFT diagonalizes — that diagonalization is what makes
-- the circulant solve `x = IDFT(DFT(b)/λ)` work (the solve itself is the Rust
-- omega-core::circulant module, validated there).
--
-- **3 qubits only.** This is the ripple-carry incrementer written as three
-- unrolled gates. A general `CyclicShift(n)` would need an n−1-control MCX
-- ladder, which the available gate set (CCX = 2 controls, no ancilla) cannot
-- express — so the circuit is honestly fixed at n=3, not falsely parameterized.
-- The carry cascade uses OLD low bits as controls, hence CCX→CX→X order, q[0] LSB.

@assert unitary

circuit CyclicShift() {
    qreg q[3]
    creg c[3]

    apply CCX on q[0], q[1], q[2]   -- carry into bit 2 when bits 0,1 are set
    apply CX on q[0], q[1]          -- carry into bit 1 when bit 0 is set
    apply X on q[0]                 -- flip bit 0
}
